     ssnndd__nneeoommaaggiicc — NeoMagic 256AV/ZX bridge device driver

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     To compile this driver into the kernel, place the following lines in your
     kernel configuration file:

           ddeevviiccee ssoouunndd
           ddeevviiccee ssnndd__nneeoommaaggiicc

     Alternatively, to load the driver as a module at boot time, place the
     following line in loader.conf(5):

           snd_neomagic_load="YES"

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ssnndd__nneeoommaaggiicc bridge driver allows the generic audio driver, sound(4),
     to attach to the NeoMagic 256AV/ZX audio devices.  These chips are mostly
     found in laptop computers.

HHAARRDDWWAARREE
     The ssnndd__nneeoommaaggiicc driver supports the following audio devices:

     ••   NeoMagic 256AV
     ••   NeoMagic 256ZX

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     sound(4)

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The ssnndd__nneeoommaaggiicc device driver first appeared in FreeBSD 4.0.

